From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:22:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] base: keep the release version out of //base

Release builds rewrite chrome/VERSION for every respin (ADR 0007). Two
//base actions read it: check_version_internal, for MAJOR, and
version_info, whose values patches/0012 already overrides with the
Chromium release. Each rewrite reran both; their regenerated headers
rebuilt base and relinked every host tool on top of it (protoc's
plugins, the DXC and V8 generators, transport_security_state_generator),
which then regenerated everything they write. With the build timestamp
(build/args/release.gn), that made a respin of an official build about
18,000 actions, five hours. Both actions now take MAJOR..PATCH from
//ghost/build/version.gni, the Chromium release, which changes only
with the pin. Their outputs are unchanged.

Why: process_version reads chrome/VERSION unconditionally in //base,
with no way for an embedder to give base another version file.
Upstream: not upstreamable: upstream builds chrome/VERSION's release
from scratch or through a content-addressed cache

Signed-off-by: robyroro <41092915+robyroro@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/base/BUILD.gn b/base/BUILD.gn
index ddcc03bf9bec0c0b8d32eabbf01cddd269c887b7..9c178ad963447d89e8dad5cd805985ad66b75693 100644
--- a/base/BUILD.gn
+++ b/base/BUILD.gn
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ import("//build/nocompile.gni")
 import("//build/rust/rust_static_library.gni")
 import("//build/util/process_version.gni")
 import("//build_overrides/build.gni")
+import("//ghost/build/version.gni")
 import("//testing/libfuzzer/fuzzer_test.gni")
 import("//testing/test.gni")
 import("//third_party/protobuf/proto_library.gni")
@@ -6490,8 +6491,11 @@ process_version("check_version_internal") {
   # doesn't need to build base_unittests. If this is required in the future, but
   # we haven't moved chrome/VERSION, we should ifdef out those tests.
   if (build_with_chromium) {
-    sources = [ "//chrome/VERSION" ]
-    extra_args = [
+    # Ghost: MAJOR from the Chromium release, not chrome/VERSION, which release
+    # builds rewrite for every respin (ADR 0007). Read here, it reran this action
+    # and relinked every host tool built on //base, regenerating their outputs.
+    extra_args = ghost_chromium_version_args
+    extra_args += [
       "-e",
       "VERSION_MAJOR=\"%s\" % (MAJOR)",
       "-e",
diff --git a/base/version_info/BUILD.gn b/base/version_info/BUILD.gn
index 5847ef41f696fa67f6a72794eb9ea6955e35447f..0ea7ec20d9e21365b94b84ef023e6dcfa705dba4 100644
--- a/base/version_info/BUILD.gn
+++ b/base/version_info/BUILD.gn
@@ -41,13 +41,15 @@ static_library("version_string") {
 process_version("generate_version_info") {
   template_file = "version_info_values.h.version"
   sources = [
-    "//chrome/VERSION",
     branding_file_path,
     lastchange_file,
   ]
   output = "$target_gen_dir/version_info_values.h"
 
   # Ghost: report the Chromium release, not chrome/VERSION's release version
-  # (ADR 0007), to everything that reads version_info.
+  # (ADR 0007), to everything that reads version_info. These arguments set
+  # every value chrome/VERSION would, so it isn't read: release builds rewrite
+  # it for every respin, and as an input it reran this action and recompiled
+  # whatever includes version_info.
   extra_args = ghost_chromium_version_args
 }
